    "markdown": "# Viewing files\n![](/images/r_read.png){style=\"width:400px; background:white; border-radius:5px\" fig-align=\"center\"}\n\nIn the [objects part](/objects/data_frames_matrices.qmd#creating-a-data-frame) we created <u id='data_frame_tooltip'>__data frames__</u> with R <u id='function_tooltip'>__functions__</u>. \nThis was useful to help understand how <u id='data_frame_tooltip'>__data frames__</u> work in R. \nHowever, in real life you will most likely not do this very often. \nInstead you will have data files you need to analyse with R.\n\nYou can get your data into R by having R __read__ your file.\n\nBefore reading in a file is important to know how a file is structured.\nWe'll carry this out by viewing the file with RStudio.\n\n## Directory and file setup\n\nPrior to using a file you will need to acquire it. \n\n- Make a directory/folder called \"Chapter_6\" within your main directory/folder for this workshop. \n- Download the file [Liverpool_beaches.csv](https://neof-workshops.github.io/R_j4c0xh/downloads/Liverpool_beaches.csv) into \"Chapter_6\". \n- Set your working directory to this new directory ([set working directory](http://localhost:3406/foundations/directories.html#commands)). You will stay here for this part\n\n## Viewing the file\n![](/images/view.png){style=\"width:200px; background:white; border-radius:5px\" fig-align=\"center\"}\n\nIn the next page we'll __read__ in the file \"Liverpool_beaches.csv\". \nBefore __reading__ in the file we can check the contents of the file. \nThis can be carried out by opening it with notepad (or similar text tool) or viewing the file with RStudio. \n\nTo view the file with RStudio:\n\n- Use the __Files pane__ of the __MISC window__ to navigate to the directory containing the file\n- Click on the file name and then click \"View File\"\n- This will open a tab in the __Source window__ matching the file name\n\nYou will notice that the values/fields/columns are separated by commas as this is a \"comma separated value\" (.csv) file. Additionally, this is the same data as the \"beach_df_2\" <u id='data_frame_tooltip'>__data frame__</u> you created in the [object exercises](/objects/exercise.qmd).\n\n::: {.callout-note}\nCreate a new R script file called __\"3-Files_and_subsetting.r\"__ for this chapter's scripts.\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-0ff0eda7b09c189130d4\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-0ff0eda7b09c189130d4\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"operator_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"+, -, /, *, etc.\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-5713c24ecd249a4d7ea9\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-5713c24ecd249a4d7ea9\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"variable_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Container of an R object with a name\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-32a50f42e4452eed0370\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-32a50f42e4452eed0370\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"function_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Named block of code that performs a specific task\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-117c19a129e982e03c36\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-117c19a129e982e03c36\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"class_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Object data type, e.g. integer, double, string, and logical\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-b7801194d17dbe109a42\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-b7801194d17dbe109a42\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"data_structure_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Object structure type, e.g. scalar, vector, and data frame\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-493c530207646448b99e\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-493c530207646448b99e\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"integer_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Number without decimal points\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-06b038ea1af2fe63cc6b\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-06b038ea1af2fe63cc6b\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"double_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Number with decimal points\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-fill-item\" height=\"464px\" id=\"htmlwidget-c808762e960f1db6f9cc\" width=\"100%\"></span>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-c808762e960f1db6f9cc\">{\"x\":{\"element\":\"string_tooltip\",\"opts\":{\"content\":\"Text\",\"arrow\":true,\"placement\":\"bottom\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<span class=\"tippy html-widget html-f